{"id": "EUVD-2026-108903", "enisaUuid": "5c261ee0-f3a9-34af-b696-ebd1fca95cea", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmtd: spinand: fix NULL pointer dereference with no ECC engine\n\nWhen \"nand-no-ecc-engine\" is set in DT, nanddev_get_ecc_engine() takes\nthe NAND_ECC_ENGINE_TYPE_NONE path and returns success while leaving\nnand->ecc.engine NULL. The SPI-NAND code nevertheless dereferences it\nunconditionally to test for a pipelined engine, so probing such a\ndevice oopses immediately.\n\nRather than open-coding the test three times, add a\nnand_ecc_is_pipelined() helper to the NAND core that folds the NULL\ncheck into the integration comparison, and use it everywhere. Future\ncallers then cannot reintroduce the problem.", "datePublished": "2026-10-23T12:11:34", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-23T12:11:34", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/77c449c9c946fc420008dc55cd30f53749c915e4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3c765fd5212c1bbc71568b1518a7ec963a7040b4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/80e8b0ea73ba295e92dfb6cf1c41df9da64234c6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fc2f651f520394893b14b75281a01e502bfa73bb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b890e6163761ddb580cc74f43e15f8bbde15647e"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98931"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0005250f-29c2-307d-8684-340e68dd55a5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f9d7c7265bcff7d9a17425a8cddf702e8fe159c2 <3c765fd5212c1bbc71568b1518a7ec963a7040b4"}, {"id": "1cbbb147-5317-3286-86ad-7497454586ef", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f9d7c7265bcff7d9a17425a8cddf702e8fe159c2 <b890e6163761ddb580cc74f43e15f8bbde15647e"}, {"id": "1d5d7ae4-dc2a-35d4-834b-338dc7e2df39", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.10"}, {"id": "22bf4f82-8033-3f90-867c-e7317360f56a", "product": {"name": "Linux"